### =====================================================================
### Web API request messages.
###
### The state-changing student endpoints require an authenticated session and
### a CSRF token. Sign in first with the request below; IntelliJ keeps the
### JSESSIONID cookie in its cookie jar for the requests that follow.
### =====================================================================

### Sign in as advisor1 (owns students 1 and 2) -- 302 Found
POST http://localhost:8080/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=advisor1&password=advisor123

### Sign in as admin -- 302 Found
POST http://localhost:8080/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=admin&password=admin123


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### GET a single student
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Fetching one student - OK (200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/students/1
Accept: application/json

### Fetching one student - Not Found (404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/students/999
Accept: application/json


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### GET the student collection (search) - used by the Client project
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Searching for students - OK (200, one or more matches)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/students?name=ali
Accept: application/json

### Searching for students - OK (200, empty array)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/students?name=zzzzz
Accept: application/json

### Listing all students - OK (200, no query parameter)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/students
Accept: application/json


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST a new student
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Creating a student - Created (201, note the Location response header)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/students
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Eve Developer",
  "yearOfStudy": 1
}

### Creating a student - Bad Request (400: blank name and yearOfStudy > 7)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/students
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "yearOfStudy": 10
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### PATCH a student's GPA
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Updating student GPA - OK (200, signed in as the owning advisor or admin)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/students/1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "gpa": 3.9
}

### Updating student GPA - Bad Request (400: GPA > 4.0)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/students/1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "gpa": 5.5
}

### Updating student GPA - Forbidden (403: sign in as advisor1, who does not own student 3)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/students/3
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "gpa": 3.9
}

### Updating student GPA - Not Found (404)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/students/999
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "gpa": 3.9
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### DELETE a student
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Deleting a student - No Content (204, signed in as the owning advisor or admin)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/students/2
Accept: application/json

### Deleting a student - Forbidden (403: sign in as advisor1, who does not own student 3)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/students/3
Accept: application/json

### Deleting a student - Not Found (404)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/students/999
Accept: application/json


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST a housing unit (week 10: permitAll + CSRF disabled for the Client)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Creating a housing unit - Created (201, note the Location response header)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/units
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "address": "99 Client Way",
  "capacity": 3,
  "rent": 700.0,
  "unitType": "STUDIO",
  "furnished": true,
  "imageUrl": "https://placehold.co/300x200?text=Client+Unit"
}

### Creating a housing unit - Bad Request (400: blank address, capacity < 1, negative rent)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/units
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "address": "",
  "capacity": 0,
  "rent": -5.0,
  "unitType": ""
}
